This directory contains source code to the following tools:

DATABASE COMPILERS
================================================================================
ccdbase		- Used to compile the database. Should only be invoked from the
		  top-level Makefile with "make dbase"

ccauthors	- Used to compile AUTHORS. Should only be used from ccdbase.

ccawards	- Used to compile various award files. Should only be used
		  from ccdbase.

ccinterv	- Used to compile INTERVIEWS. Should only be used from ccdbase.

ccpubs		- Used to compile various publication files. Should only be used
		  from ccdbase.

ccreviews	- Used to compile REVIEWS. Should only be used from ccdbase.

cctitles	- Used to compile various title files. Should only be used 
		  from ccdbase.

info		- Used to generate compile-time statistics.



DATABASE MERGING TOOLS
================================================================================
Note: The tools are only briefly described here. Refer to the FAQ for
a more in-depth tutorial on how to use these tools.
================================================================================
merge		- One of the most-used merging tools. When given a file in
		  title format (SHORTFICTION, ESSAYS, COLLECTIONS, ANTHOLOGIES,
		  etc...), it scans the file for duplicate entries (entries
		  that have identical titles and authors) and merges them.

lexint		- Searches a file in title format for possible inexact duplicates.
		  Used to find titles that have subtle lexical differences. This 
		  will output both titles like this:

		  --------------------------------
		  [Adelard's Kiss] by [Madeleine E. Robins] AND
		  [Abelard's Kiss] by [Madeleine E. Robins]
		  --------------------------------

		  This should be used on a new database file before trying to
		  compare the entries to those already in the ISFDB.

lexext		- This is very similar to lexint, except that it compares the 
		  entries in a new dabase file to those in an ISFDB file. 
		  Usage is:

			lexext <isfdb file> <new file>

pubint		- Intended to find duplicate publication entries in the ISFDB.
		  You shouldn't need this for database merging.

pubext		- Finds differences in publication data between the ISFDB and
		  the new database. The ISFDB and the new database *must* be in
		  agreement before a merge can be completed. For each publication
		  that is in agreement, a key mapping is emitted into the KEYMAP
		  file.

content		- Compares the content of antholgies or collections between the
		  ISFDB and the new database. It only checks entries that have
		  mappings in the KEYMAP file.

newdb		- One the ISFDB and the new database are in agreement, the newdb
		  application will build a new set of database files. These
		  consist of the new database, minus those entries which the ISFDB
		  and the new database alreay have in common (they don't need to
		  be merged into the ISFDB since they are already there).



UTILITIES
================================================================================
booksort	- This binary works like "sort" except that entries are sorted
		  in booksort order. Leading articles are ignored. Note that
		  this binary only works on compiled data files; it will not
		  work with files in ISFDB data format.

cap		- This binary examines titles in ISFDB database files, and whines
		  about those titles which might contain improperly capitalized
		  words. This binary only works on files in titles format; it
		  can't parse awards, reviews, interviews, or publication data.

		  "cap ESSAYS" will give output similar to:

		  --------------------------------------------------------
		  FROM: [The Next Man on The Moon] (James E. Oberg)
		  TO:   [The next Man on the Moon]
		  --------------------------------------------------------
		  FROM: [Life is in The Stars] (Thomas A. Easton)
		  TO:   [Life is in the Stars]

checkauthors	- This tools finds bad canonical author names. It uses the file
		  BADAUTH as a basis for unacceptable names. Helps to find author
		  names that are actually pseudonyms plus those that are 
		  commonly misspelled.

fixessays	- This tool examines the ESSAYS file and looks for generic
		  titles like "Introduction", "Preface", "Editorial", etc...
		  It then looks up the publication it was published in and
		  changes the title to "Introduction (Ascents of Wonder)".
		  Since this tools looks at publication data in dbase.compiled,
		  the database must be compiled prior to using this tool.

pubdups		- This tools examines a titles file for publication tag
		  duplicates.

tileawards      - this application is used on the award_template file in htmls.
		  Since the award.html file uses radio buttons in alphabetical
		  order, it's difficult to add a new award by hand to the file.
		  Instead the award is added to award_template, and tileawards
		  will transform the information into html radio button format.
